Templeton Protect — licensing
==============================

The scanning ENGINE and command-line tool are MIT-licensed, under the terms
below. This is everything that finds and explains a finding: mac/Sources/
ProtectCore, mac/Sources/CLI, the exports, and the test suites.

The RESIDENT APPLICATION LAYER — the menu bar presence, scheduled scanning and
the transcript watcher, in mac/Sources/Protect/Resident.swift, Watcher.swift and
Plan.swift — is part of Protect+, a commercial product. It is published here to
be read and audited; running it as a service is offered by subscription. See
docs/PRODUCT.md.

Nothing in the MIT engine depends on the resident layer, and the free scanner is
complete on its own. This split is stated here, in the first paragraph, on
purpose — an "open source" badge over a paid core is the misread this project
refuses to earn.

